<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russia says Europe bought $320 billion in hydrocarbons since 2022</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8dcdab1db2a26f70e684669fe1a45ec7bd1ec415c51195de9b8cb917e215f43</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T03:10:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-says-europe-bought-320-billion-in-hydrocarbons-since-2022" /><summary type="html">Russia said on Monday that European Union countries had bought $320.7 billion worth of its energy resources since 2022, despite sanctions over the war in Ukraine. The figure fuelled tensions as European officials criticised a US deal to import Russian diesel, while Stockholm called for the bloc to use frozen Russian assets to boost support for Kyiv.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Breaking Bad' actor and disability activist RJ Mitte dies aged 34</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ba358652ceaca7a1afacac768027ac99bacec73c2c60b8620e4c0537776fd61</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T01:43:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-breaking-bad-actor-and-disability-activist-rj-mitte-dies-aged-34" /><summary type="html">"Breaking Bad" actor RJ Mitte, who played Walter White Jr. in the hit US television series, has died aged 34, his representatives said Monday. The actor, who lived with cerebal palsy, also became a prominent disability rights advocate, championing inclusion and representation in film and television.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo to enter hospital on Tuesday for surgery on lung nodule this week</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:039ea501fe4e0488879b8d5c8e5555bbf897ba333fb1354bdf6284fdffa6db67</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T22:20:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-planned-lung-operation-this-week" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV is expected to undergo surgery to remove a lung nodule this week at Rome’s Gemelli hospital, with doctors anticipating a recovery of about seven days. The 71-year-old pontiff is due to travel to Uruguay, Argentina and Peru on November 6, though the Vatican has not confirmed the operation date.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French supermarkets suffer refrigerator shutdown after 'unprecedented' cyberattack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc628b45c4d9db75747e64784d4e21881f3bf066907c9417f70e319c8a289eab</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T21:27:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-supermarkets-suffer-refrigerator-shutdown-after-unprecedented-cyberattack" /><summary type="html">Major French supermarket chains on Monday said they were hit by a cyberattack that caused their refrigerators to shoot up in temperature in hundreds of stores, forcing spoiled food to be thrown away and raising concerns about food security. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo’s former president Kabila to lead new movement with M23 rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4b36d2a23835f27cf64bbe2f319d0b218a0b091f8ceabca7357435c082f3917</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T21:27:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261012-dr-congo-former-president-joseph-kabila-to-lead-new-movement-with-m23-rebels" /><summary type="html">Former DR Congo president Joseph Kabila announced a new political-military alliance with Rwanda-backed M23 rebels on Monday, despite being sentenced to death in absentia for alleged complicity with the group. The move comes as debate grows over constitutional changes ahead of President Felix Tshisekedi’s final term ending in 2028.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Paris Motor Show kicks off as China-EU rivalry heats up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c373f2b9098a2728542cf85211cecef835c8524e9c9633256bdbef940e5d027a</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T21:03:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261012-paris-motor-show-kicks-off-as-china-eu-rivalry-heats-up" /><summary type="html">The biennial Paris Motor Show kicks off with a record number of Chinese brands descending on the French capital.  European carmakers are fighting back, showcasing their latest models, as the EU announced a deal with China to limit the imports of hybrids.  France 24's Charles Pellegrin has been speaking with CEOs of both Chinese and European carmakers.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>'It's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington', analyst says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e342e9f0823ce797445d4d481593c452ba9189f95dd14891409920b8c446dfa5</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T21:02:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261012-it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump's envoys told ​Ukrainian officials on Friday that a deal to allow Russian diesel exports is part of a bid to draw Russia back to negotiations after the failure of previous efforts to launch sustained talks to end the war, three people familiar with the meeting told Reuters. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Grégoire Roos, director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. He says that "it's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington because Vladimir Putin knows that Donald Trump lives on borrowed time".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>No, these pictures do not show the Houthi attacks on Riyadh King Khalid Airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a5a108c95b0d93c2888982706c72efc5eb7cd9fff90ac34924d536e61f0dc5a</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:59:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261012-no-these-pictures-do-not-show-the-houthi-attacks-on-riyadh-king-khalid-airport" /><summary type="html">As Saudi Arabia’s King Khalid International Airport has suffered a string of deadly attacks, claimed by the Houthis, a slew of AI-generated or decontextualised videos and photos have been circulating on social media, purporting to show the strikes of the last few days.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'It's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington', analyst says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e52fe271edb0333ca52838045a75f59dcf2de3ffa161603756ae65438267d5df</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:58:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump's envoys told ​Ukrainian officials on Friday that a deal to allow Russian diesel exports is part of a bid to draw Russia back to negotiations after the failure of previous efforts to launch sustained talks to end the war, three people familiar with the meeting told Reuters. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Grégoire Roos, director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. He says that "it's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington because Vladimir Putin knows that Donald Trump lives on borrowed time".</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian govt forces enter key Tigray town near Eritrea border</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a854d9ef1a1e9d533195bdaaec902a246392538966bf1f0f2ed7d28ed71223d3</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:34:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-govt-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-near-eritrea-border" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Ethiopian forces tighten their grip on Tigray, advancing into the key town of Adwa after rebels withdrew. Also, police arrested 30 people amid violence across South Africa. And we head to Tunisia, where ancient Sufi chants collide with pulsating electronic beats!</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Tehran denies involvement in UK Fairford air base incident as Britain summons Iranian ambassador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:961b13ee5fb31056f2aa96b2be273e1b76b7d3053e76896ae2ce05d7d0c83da6</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:23:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-tehran-denies-involvement-in-uk-fairford-air-base-incident-as-britain-summons-iranian-ambassador" /><summary type="html">British Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Monday accused Iran's Revolutionary Guards of being responsible for a terror-related incident in September at England's Fairford air base, which is used by the United States military. Following Tehran's denial, the British Foreign Office summoned Iran's Ambassador for talks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French presidential hopeful Glucksmann says 'battle begins' to revive divided left</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a28d4bfa5d0a95efad5aa30c0d82efa4303ec2fcb231f3c54c0286b99c730183</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:18:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-presidential-hopeful-glucksmann-says-battle-begins-to-revive-divided-left" /><summary type="html">French presidential candidate Raphael Glucksmann declared Monday that the "battle begins" as he launched a bid to unite a fragmented left ahead of next year's election. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Damien Lecomte, Political Scientist and Researcher at Paris Pantheon Sorbonne University, explains that Glucksmann has to be careful not to be seen as "the new Macron, because that is not a winning card".</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthi official warns of 'swift, painful response' if US enters Yemen war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65862cdc5972a5721def0066ea81ff0488229640e6fd05d6a391ed1086efc725</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:42:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/houthi-official-warns-of-swift-painful-response-if-us-enters-yemen-war" /><summary type="html">A Houthi official on Monday warned the US it would receive a "painful response" if it entered the war in Yemen, where Saudi Arabia has reportedly requested Washington's help in dealing with the group as it weathers repeated attacks. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Increasingly evident' Russia won't accept 'energy ceasefire': Zelensky</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cf0426b0de49883d801baa93c54ab1b2758d1423170ae026d804cf6512cfc87</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:40:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/increasingly-evident-russia-won-t-accept-energy-ceasefire-zelensky" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday it was clear that Russia would not agree to stop hitting energy targets, after US President Donald Trump unilaterally announced a deal between the warring nations. "It is increasingly evident that Russia is unwilling to accept an energy ceasefire proposed by the United States," Zelensky said on social media. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis 'are thriving and surviving by creating war', Yemen ambassador says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa77b23f58bc3df0f27896b3d8222b9cb08c69f9af30d1b7e8443fce85ba9ef4</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:08:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/houthis-are-thriving-and-surviving-by-creating-war-yemen-ambassador-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Yemen's ambassador to France Riyad Yassin Abdallah says that the Iran-backed Houthi "are thriving and surviving by creating war". Saudi Arabia's energy minister on Monday said the country had been tested but would mount a "serious" response after a string of attacks on Riyadh's international airport by Yemen's Houthis that left 18 people dead.</summary></entry><entry><title>'A lot of Ukrainians are feeling extremely betrayed' by Trump's Russian diesel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f19addd5be957c1db0a781be5009f5597fd37c10c5642f9dbc39da770adcfb35</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:04:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-lot-of-ukrainians-are-feeling-extremely-betrayed-by-trump-s-russian-diesel-deal" /><summary type="html">Reporting from central Ukraine, FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg says that "a lot of Ukrainians are feeling extremely betrayed by a country that until recently they saw not only as an ally but as a beacon of freedom and democracy, a country whose values they should aspire to. All of that is falling apart very quickly and Ukrainians' admiration for the United States is disintegrating."</summary></entry><entry><title>How exposed is Saudi Arabia? Yemen's Houthis scale up drone and missile attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78800e91695d28c758668c235eadd4147e06c3375155fd87fc6516b35f60aa26</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T18:33:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261012-how-exposed-is-saudi-arabia-yemen-s-houthis-scale-up-drone-and-missile-attacks" /><summary type="html">How exposed is Saudi Arabia? Just as Iran’s retaliation to Donald Trump’s war suddenly exposed the vulnerability of neighboring Gulf states…how much is Riyadh reeling from the escalation with Yemen’s Tehran-backed Houthis? We’ll assess the physical and material damage from strikes on airports and oil facilities as well as eventual repercussions for the kingdom’s ability to project strength. In the age of cheap drone warfare, how much can a battle-hardened militia push against the region’s richest nation?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>French presidential candidate Glucksmann says 'battle begins' to unite fragmented left</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e440981ffa6549bdbfaa8654bb0b715217618319027d13d4cc4b21108cc6db3</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T17:07:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261012-french-presidential-candidate-glucksmann-says-battle-begins-to-unite-fragmented-left--59d3b747ae6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261012-french-presidential-candidate-glucksmann-says-battle-begins-to-unite-fragmented-left" /><summary type="html">French presidential candidate Raphaël Glucksmann said Monday that the "battle begins" to revive the country's divided left ahead of the 2027 election. The EU lawmaker was elected Sunday as the centre-left candidate with more than 66 percent of the vote.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France: Fire destroys historic covered food market in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07631ac7c7319aef3b521df71bc3c1a2d944d2a609e0f6d70be6b3daed0c18bf</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:23:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-fire-destroys-historic-covered-food-market-in-paris--e9a2dc436f25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-fire-destroys-historic-covered-food-market-in-paris" /><summary type="html">The iconic Marché des Enfants-Rouges in Paris was ravaged by fire overnight. Adored by locals and tourists alike, it was believed to be the oldest food market in Paris. There were no casualties, but the market’s vendors have lost everything, and the history is irreplaceable. Details by Charli James.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands of Indians march to Supreme Court to oust election chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e061501e81c628634b1180c8d2ec102b62af4b1bdc1fbd428ebb4ec796e718a</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:23:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief--cfcf565f6afb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief" /><summary type="html">Protesters in New Delhi continue to take to the streets demanding the country's top election commissioner resign. Frustrations have been mounting after an investigation in a leading newspaper revealed concerns had been raised within the body, over the revision of voter lists. Delano D'Souza reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia extends Riyadh aiport suspension, vows deadly response to Houthis strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf07710d326a3448d65a508c80320662082842cac8d46d75deecb977d22fb26c</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:21:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-extends-riyadh-aiport-suspension-vows-deadly-response-to-houthis-strikes--faba784fd28a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-extends-riyadh-aiport-suspension-vows-deadly-response-to-houthis-strikes" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia extended on Monday the closure of the international airport in Riyadh after announcing the Saudi-led coalition was responding to Houthi combined drone and missile attacks. On Saturday, another attack left 13 dead and over 300 injured. This is one of the worst disruptions to Saudi aviation in years – marking a significant escalation in the war with Yemen's Houthi rebels. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Philip Turle.</summary></entry><entry><title>Chinese cars vs Europe: Who will win the battle for the market?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:491b18e26b751ca7caffcc2a9e2ea26332e9c857b373bc26484179b8adc1e4f8</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:20:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/chinese-cars-vs-europe-who-will-win-the-battle-for-the-market--488a396b2ae3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/chinese-cars-vs-europe-who-will-win-the-battle-for-the-market" /><summary type="html">The biennial Paris Motor Show officially opened this Monday in France. Over 200 auto sector brands will be present, rivalling for attention with their latest models and innovations. This competition for attention mirrors the competition for market share. This is especially true between local European brands and Chinese ones which have seen their sales surge on the continent over the past ten years – prompting accusations of unfair competition. Report by Charles Pellegrin, FRANCE 24’s business editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>The revival of a classic: Citroën unveils new electric version of its 2CV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94c2f00f179a8651cf5d1a8269e8e7f0750d0f69f42ed8e11b1c862da4d81f0a</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:08:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-the-revival-of-a-classic-citro_n-unveils-new-electric-version-of-its-2cv--4f85fd5fec58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-the-revival-of-a-classic-citro%C3%ABn-unveils-new-electric-version-of-its-2cv" /><summary type="html">French car manufacturer Citroën has unveiled a new electric version of its classic 2CV. Although still a concept vehicle, the company says it plans to put the car into production within the next two years.</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms 2026: Turning Point and the battle for Charlie Kirk’s legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b658381dbe01e0216aa75a63030c105b805a0d74c2609a10ba64785bfe6be26</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T15:59:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-midterms-2026-turning-point-and-the-battle-for-charlie-kirk-s-legacy--d6085c6fb972.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-midterms-2026-turning-point-and-the-battle-for-charlie-kirk-s-legacy" /><summary type="html">In the year following the death of Charlie Kirk, the number of American universities with Turning Point chapters surged by 64 percent. But at the same time there have been signs of division in the organisation Kirk founded and the MAGA movement more generally: far-right figures are vying for Kirk’s legacy, while conspiracy theories circulate regarding his death. But as the midterms approach, how do activists on the ground see the future of the conservative youth movement? And who, if anyone, can take on Kirk’s mantle? France 24 travelled to the place Turning Point was founded - Phoenix, Arizona - to find out more.</summary></entry></feed>
